# Swan Compiler 2 — SIL Generation
#
# Swift-inspired SILGen: lower the typed AST into Swan Intermediate Language.
# SIL is a high-level, typed, ownership-aware compiler IR. It is not machine
# code, bytecode for an interpreter, or a target-specific representation.
#
# Responsibilities:
# - Lower declarations, expressions, statements, and control flow.
# - Represent values in SSA form with explicit basic blocks and terminators.
# - Make ownership operations and lifetime boundaries explicit.
# - Preserve source locations for diagnostics and debug information.
# - Represent calls, allocations, projections, and memory accesses explicitly.
# - Produce deterministic SIL independent of the selected CPU architecture.
#
# Output must pass the SIL verifier before any SIL analysis or optimization.
# Unsupported AST nodes are hard errors.
#
# Implementation status: contract; no complete AST-to-SIL lowering yet.
